<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Bids down, selling slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat- Bids down, selling slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bids for dark northern spring wheat fell on Monday, in line with losses in the MGE spring wheat futures, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers noted a lack of farm sales and farmers preparing fields for seeding in various parts of the Northern Plains states.</p>
<p>More farmers were planting, and spring wheat plantings were about on time, a Montana merchandiser said.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures ended weaker on spillover pressure from other markets and on improved planting prospects in the northern U.S. Plains, traders said.</p>
<p>MGE May spring futures lost eight cents to $4.32-1/2 a bushel.  </p>
